OL,3,AWorker paralysed in 30ft fall from
OL,4,Apylon gets #10m payout
OL,5,
OL,6,FA maintenance worker whose life was
OL,7,F"turned upside down" when he fell 30ft
OL,8,Ffrom a power line and was left
OL,9,Fparalysed has won at least #10m in
OL,10,Fcompensation.
OL,12,FGavin Pugh was dismantling a pylon in
OL,13,FApril 2022 when he unknowingly clipped
OL,14,Fhis safety line to a section that was
OL,15,Fonly secure at one end.
OL,17,FHis safety rope slipped loose, causing
OL,18,Fhim to plunge to the ground and suffer
OL,19,Flife-changing injuries to his brain,
OL,20,Fneck, shoulder, ribs and internal
OL,21,Forgans which mean he needs a wheelchair
OL,22,Ffor the rest of his life.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,310,300,200,140,0,100
